2025-05-01 03:29:44 - Thread-1465 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant tables, columns, and how we will use them  

Match."home_team_api_id":  identify the home‑side team in each match  
Match."away_team_api_id":  identify the away‑side team in each match  
Match."home_team_goal":     number of goals scored by the home team – used to detect a home win  
Match."away_team_goal":     number of goals scored by the away team – used to detect an away win  
Team."team_api_id":         primary key that lets us join a team to a match row  
Team."team_long_name":      readable team name to be shown in the final list  

Main conditions that will be useful  

• Home win  ->  Match."home_team_goal"  >  Match."away_team_goal"  
• Away win  ->  Match."away_team_goal"  >  Match."home_team_goal"  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries (use any or all as needed).  
Every query is a pure SELECT, uses DISTINCT when appropriate, and is capped with LIMIT 20.  
Replace … with any extra filters you may want.

```sql
--1 Description: Inspect a handful of matches to see the raw goal columns.
SELECT "id", "home_team_api_id", "away_team_api_id",
       "home_team_goal", "away_team_goal"
FROM "Match"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2 Description: Look at matches in which the home side clearly won.
SELECT "id", "home_team_api_id", "away_team_api_id",
       "home_team_goal", "away_team_goal"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3 Description: Look at matches in which the away side clearly won.
SELECT "id", "home_team_api_id", "away_team_api_id",
       "home_team_goal", "away_team_goal"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "away_team_goal" > "home_team_goal"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4 Description: List 20 distinct team IDs that appear as the home side.
SELECT DISTINCT "home_team_api_id"
FROM "Match"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5 Description: Preview 20 readable team names from the Team table.
SELECT DISTINCT "team_api_id", "team_long_name"
FROM "Team"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6 Description: Join Match→Team to see who was the winning HOME team (sample).
SELECT  m."id" AS match_id,
        t."team_long_name" AS home_winner,
        m."home_team_goal", m."away_team_goal"
FROM "Match" AS m
JOIN "Team"  AS t
  ON m."home_team_api_id" = t."team_api_id"
WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7 Description: Count how many HOME‑field wins each team has (top 20).
SELECT  t."team_long_name",
        COUNT(*) AS home_wins
FROM "Match" AS m
JOIN "Team"  AS t
  ON m."home_team_api_id" = t."team_api_id"
WHERE m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
GROUP BY t."team_long_name"
ORDER BY home_wins DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8 Description: Count how many AWAY‑field wins each team has (top 20).
SELECT  t."team_long_name",
        COUNT(*) AS away_wins
FROM "Match" AS m
JOIN "Team"  AS t
  ON m."away_team_api_id" = t."team_api_id"
WHERE m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
GROUP BY t."team_long_name"
ORDER BY away_wins DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--9 Description: Combine home & away wins for a complete win tally per team (sample top 20).
SELECT  t."team_long_name",
        SUM(CASE WHEN m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal" THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) +
        SUM(CASE WHEN m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal" THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS total_wins
FROM "Match" AS m
JOIN "Team"  AS t
     ON t."team_api_id" IN (m."home_team_api_id", m."away_team_api_id")
GROUP BY t."team_long_name"
ORDER BY total_wins DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10 Description: Final answer – Top‑10 teams with the most overall wins across the whole dataset.
SELECT  t."team_long_name"        AS team,
        COUNT(*)                  AS wins
FROM (
        SELECT "home_team_api_id" AS team_id
        FROM "Match"
        WHERE "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal"
        UNION ALL
        SELECT "away_team_api_id" AS team_id
        FROM "Match"
        WHERE "away_team_goal" > "home_team_goal"
     ) AS w
JOIN "Team" AS t
  ON w.team_id = t."team_api_id"
GROUP BY t."team_long_name"
ORDER BY wins DESC
LIMIT 10;
```
